Fix a null dereference in get_app_name when argv[0] has no slash.

SDL_strrchr returns NULL when the command line holds no '/', and the code
adds one to it before testing, so the test sees 0x1 and strlen reads
address one. The comment says "absolute worst case we get to a '\0'",
which is true only when a slash was found.

A Flatpak launches the game as "abuse-vrenna", with no path at all, so
this crashed on the first run of the packaged build. Running it as
./build/release/src/abuse never did, and neither did gdb, which execs the
binary by its full path.

Reported upstream: libsdl-org/SDL_native_midi.

--- a/src/SDL_native_midi_alsa.c
+++ b/src/SDL_native_midi_alsa.c
@@ -269,8 +269,9 @@
     int fd = open(procfs_path, O_RDONLY);
     if (fd >= 0) {
         if (read(fd, cmdline, pathmax) > 0) {
-            char *base = SDL_strrchr(cmdline, '/') + 1; /* Absolute worst case we get to a '\0' */
-            if (base) {
+            char *slash = SDL_strrchr(cmdline, '/');
+            char *base = slash ? slash + 1 : cmdline;
+            {
                 len = strlen(base);
                 if (len)
                     SDL_memmove(cmdline, base, len + 1);
